Looking at the test at line 94 in the original test file:
```typescript
it('updates an existing record by merging the body over it', async () => {
  const res = await request(appAs(true)).put('/library/virtues/v-might').send({ Tagline: 'Force' });

  expect(res.status).toBe(200);
  expect(res.body.object).toMatchObject({ Id: 'v-might', Name: 'Might', Tagline: 'Force' });
});
```

This sends `{ Tagline: 'Force' }` and expects the result to have `Name: 'Might'` (unchanged) and `Tagline: 'Force'` (the update).

For my test, I sent `{ Name: 'Changed' }` so the result would be `Name: 'Changed'` (since that's the update). Let me fix the test to match:

